{
  "_about": "Cited engineering-reference properties for everyday materials that the first-principles physics modules (surface.py/mechanical.py/stress.py/optics.py/fluid.py) do not derive. Every value is a published reference value, cited by source code below; numeric property values are facts (uncopyrightable) cited by reference, exactly like inventory/data/dimensions.json. material_profile() (field/interface/resolve.py) prefers the DERIVED physics value where one exists and falls back to these CITED values; truly unknown materials return flagged estimates. NO value here is invented — where a grade-dependent value has spread, confidence is lowered, not faked.",
  "_units": "density kg/m^3; youngs_modulus_pa, sigma_UTS_pa Pa; K_Ic_pa_sqrtm Pa*sqrt(m); n_refractive dimensionless; reflectance 0..1; viscosity_pa_s Pa*s; surface_tension_n_m N/m. Each property is {v: value, src: source-code, c: confidence}.",
  "_license": "Numeric property values are facts (uncopyrightable); cited by published reference.",
  "_sources": {
    "CRC": "CRC Handbook of Chemistry and Physics, 104th ed. (2023)",
